b.com/users/WOLFxxxxxx/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WOLFxxxxxx/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WOLFxxxxxx/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WOLFxxxxxx/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WOLFxxxxxx/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WOLFxxxxxx/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WOLFxxxxxx/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WOLFxxxxxx/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WOLFxxxxxx/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-08T22:38:09Z","updated_at":"2026-05-08T22:38:09Z","body":"\"Thank you for the clarification. If all three renderers use Reverse-Z, then there is a clear parity issue or a regression in how the depth buffer is handled in the Vulkan Mobile backend compared to Forward+.\n\nOn the same hardware, switching to the Mobile renderer results in inverted depth/Z-fighting that does not exist in Forward+. This suggests that either:\n\nThe NDC (Normalized Device Coordinates) range is not being handled consistently between the two backends.\n\nThere is a driver-specific issue with how Reverse-Z is applied to tile-based GPUs (Mobile) in Godot's current implementation.\n\nI have verified that Near and Far clip planes are within reasonable ranges. If the logic is the same, the output should be identical. Can we investigate if the depth clear value or the projection matrix math differs in the Mobile clustered implementation?\"","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4410373915/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4411598861","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/119348#issuecomment-4411598861","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119348","id":4411598861,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABBvOoDQ","user":{"login":"clayjohn","id":16521339,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTIxMzM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16521339?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn","html_url":"https://github.com/clayjohn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-09T05:31:47Z","updated_at":"2026-05-09T05:31:47Z","body":"The projection matrix is the same between the backends. Which implies that the NDC space is the same as well! So I wouldn't follow that thread to figure things out. \n\nIf you think there is a bug in the engine then please properly fill out a bug report by providing a full response  to each of the questions and provide an MRP. Trying to speculate what might be the cause based on no information is a waste of contributors time. \n\nAlso, copy-pasting the hallucinated response of an LLM is disrespectful and not helpful. ","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4411598861/reactions","total_count":3,"+1":3,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},